Put a server-file archive here to skip the download.

The client builder normally fetches the server files from the MEGA link the
server-file profile ships with. That link is a share on somebody else's MEGA
account, so one day it will stop working. When it does -- or when you would
rather not pull 1.4 GB through your VPS -- download the archive on your own PC,
copy it into this folder, and run:

    docker compose run --rm client-builder

Anything ending in .rar, .zip or .7z is picked up from here. A ready-made
Client.zip works too: it is recognised by the launcher .exe inside it and used
directly.

The file is read where it lies and never copied into the cache, so it costs no
extra disk. It is mounted read-only.

This folder is in .gitignore apart from this README -- do not commit a
gigabyte-and-a-half of somebody else's server files.
